The legal text is the unannotated Constitution of the State of South Carolina and chapters of the South Carolina Code of Laws,
as published by the South Carolina Legislative Council on www.scstatehouse.gov. The site states: "The South Carolina Code,
consisting only of Code text, numbering, history, and Effect of Amendment, Editor's, and Code Commissioner's notes may be copied
from this website at the reader's expense and effort without need for permission." and says the same of the unannotated
Constitution. The website version is not official; the print Code is.

Statutes and constitutions are works of government that carry no copyright (Georgia v. Public.Resource.Org, Inc., 590 U.S. ___, 2020).
Only the section text and its HISTORY line are taken here; the editorial notes are left out.

The arrangement of this repository, its tables, commit messages and tools are by Lexifina and may be reused under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). This repository is not legal advice
and not an official publication. Source: South Carolina Legislative Council, www.scstatehouse.gov.
